md(n,'most headers can be repeated or combined into one comma-separated line, but `Set-Cookie` **cannot be combined**,','combining repeated field lines is allowed only when the field definition permits it. `Set-Cookie` **must not be folded into one comma-separated field**,','Combination is field-specific, not a general rule.')
md(n,'| `Secure` | Only send over HTTPS |','| `Secure` | Send only over connections the browser considers secure |','Secure cookie permits browser-defined trusted localhost exception.')
md(n,'| `HttpOnly` | Hidden from JavaScript |','| `HttpOnly` | Exclude from non-HTTP cookie APIs such as document.cookie |','Precise access mechanism, not absolute token secrecy.')
md(n,'| `Partitioned` | Separate jar per top-level site |','| `Partitioned` | Add a top-level-site partition key in supporting browsers; requires Secure |','CHIPS partitions existing cookie scope; not independent of origin and security requirements.')
md(n,'and the **same** name, domain and path.','and matching name, domain/host-only scope and path, in the same partition if applicable.','6265bis includes host-only flag in identity and partitioning adds partition key.')
md(n,'makes it go to `example.com` *and every subdomain*.','allows host matching for `example.com` *and its subdomains*, subject to path, security, SameSite and browser policy. The setting host must domain-match that Domain value.','Domain matching does not override other delivery conditions or permit arbitrary domains.')
md(n,'Browsers refuse `Domain` values on the **Public Suffix List** (`co.uk`, `github.io`), so one customer cannot set cookies for all others.','Public-suffix rejection prevents a tenant from setting a parent-suffix cookie for other tenants. The algorithm has a host-only exception when the setting host itself equals the suffix; lists and browser policy matter.','RFC algorithm has explicit public-suffix-self exception.')
md(n,'a page under `/public` on the same origin can read `/admin` cookies by framing an `/admin` page via JavaScript.','same-origin script may access a matching-path document, subject to framing policy. Path does not isolate mutually distrustful applications on one origin; HttpOnly separately restricts script cookie access.','Original ignored HttpOnly and framing restrictions.')
md(n,'**Secure** means the cookie is never sent over plain HTTP. **HttpOnly** hides it from `document.cookie`. HttpOnly limits the damage of XSS (the attacker cannot steal the session token), but it does not stop XSS: injected script can still make requests that the browser decorates with the cookie.','**Secure** normally requires HTTPS; browsers may treat localhost as a trusted exception. **HttpOnly** prevents direct access through document.cookie and similar non-HTTP APIs. It does not guarantee that XSS cannot expose a token through another vulnerable application feature, and injected script can still make authenticated requests.','Avoid absolute HTTPS-only and token-theft guarantee.')
md(n,'A **site** is the scheme plus the *registrable domain* (eTLD+1):','For these ordinary domain URLs, a schemeful **site** is the scheme plus the *registrable domain* (eTLD+1):','IP/opaque origins and no-registrable-domain cases differ.')
md(n,'Following a link from an email to your bank arrives logged out.','On a cross-site navigation, that cookie is withheld from the initial request; what the user sees depends on application behaviour.','Email context and app login behaviour are not guaranteed.')
md(n,'`None`: sent everywhere, and browsers require `Secure` with it.','`None`: removes the SameSite restriction and requires Secure in supporting browsers. Domain/path rules, partitioning and third-party-cookie policies still apply.','None does not mean everyrequest carriescookie.')
md(n,'Chrome and Edge treat a cookie **without** `SameSite` as `Lax` (with a short grace window for top-level POSTs straight after the cookie is set). `Lax` blocks the classic CSRF attack, a hidden cross-site form POST, but it is defence in depth, not a replacement for CSRF tokens on state-changing GETs (which you should not have anyway).','The 6265bis draft specifies Lax-style default enforcement and allows a user-agent-chosen recent-cookie exception for cookies with no explicit SameSite value. Explicit Lax excludes that exception. SameSite helps against cross-site CSRF, but does not cover same-site sibling attacks or all application flows. Use appropriate CSRF protection for state-changing requests; GET should not perform state changes.','Separate explicitLax from default exception and avoid CSRF protection onlyforGET misconception.')
md(n,'Cookie names can carry a prefix the browser enforces:','Supporting browsers enforce cookie-name prefixes:','Prefix enforcement depends on supporting user agent.')
md(n,'This pins the cookie to exactly one host, so a compromised or careless subdomain cannot overwrite it.','This prevents a sibling from setting a parent-domain cookie under that prefixed name. It does not isolate ports on the same host or authenticate a Cookie header supplied by an arbitrary client.','Prefix is browser storage constraint, not server authenticity proof.')
md(n,'and real browsers sit close to those numbers. Every cookie in scope rides on *every* request, including image requests, so a 3 KB cookie on a page with 80 assets adds about 240 KB of upload. Serve static assets from a cookieless domain if this bites.','as recommended minimum capabilities in that RFC, not universal current limits. Cookie inclusion also depends on path, security, SameSite, credentials mode and browser policy. For 80 actual HTTP/1.1 requests each carrying 3,000 cookie bytes, the repeated values total 240,000 bytes before other overhead. Cache hits can avoid requests; HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 compression savings depend on encoder/table decisions.\n\n> [!note] Content omitted after review\n> A current browser-by-browser cookie limit, prefix-support and eviction-policy matrix is absent because those version-specific implementations were not tested here.','Avoidfalsebrowserlimits and all-requestcookie guarantee; giveexplicitcostmodel.')
md(n,'**Treating `Path` or `HttpOnly` as security.** Neither stops a determined script on the same origin.','**Treating cookie attributes as complete XSS protection.** HttpOnly is a real restriction on cookie APIs, but does not prevent injected script from making authenticated requests. Path is not an isolation boundary.','Do not dismiss genuine HttpOnly security property.')
md(n,'Body framing: no body for HEAD/1xx/204/304, then chunked, then Content-Length, then close-delimited (responses only).','Apply the ordered framing and error rules: special bodyless responses and CONNECT tunnels come before transfer coding, valid Content-Length and applicable close-delimiting.','Keep summary aligned with corrected framing.')
